WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.020
July 2019 promises to be a big month for Amazon
Prime's original and exclusive content, with

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.400
a slew of movies and television series lined
up to join the streaming service's library.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.920
Get a head start on all the additions to your
queue with our look at the month's best Amazon

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.200
Prime Video arrivals.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:22.180
While it was released in Great Britain in
October 2018, the historical drama Peterloo,

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.290
directed by Cannes Film Festival favorite
Mike Leigh, becomes available for Amazon Prime

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.900
subscribers on July 3rd.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:32.500
Peterloo chronicles a bloody massacre Britain's
military unleashed on its own people.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.120
More than a decade after the bloody Napoleonic
Wars finally ended, England was in rough shape.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:42.480
Responding to widespread poverty, unemployment,
and famine, among other ills, somewhere between

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:49.140
60,000 and 100,000 peaceful protesters gathered
in Manchester, England on August 10, 1819

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.240
to demand parliamentary reform, including
granting universal suffrage.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.200
"We shall maintain our spirits!"

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.690
The meeting was interrupted by cavalrymen
attempting to arrest the resistance leaders

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:04.760
and eventually charging into the crowds on
horseback to deadly consequences.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:12.460
In 2016's Captain America: Civil War, we saw
one potential aftermath of superheroes unintentionally

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.180
hurting innocent civilians while fighting
supervillains.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.560
When writer Garth Ennis and artist Darick
Robertson premiered their brutally amusing

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:24.109
superhero comic The Boys in 2006, they weren't
quite so forgiving.

00:01:24.109 --> 00:01:28.099
The superheroes of The Boys, for the most
part, are examples of what happens when you

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.560
give godlike physical power to the least responsible,
most twisted individuals you can find.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.140
Karl Urban stars as Billy Butcher, leader
of the vigilante group dedicated to taking

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:40.609
down the Justice-League-like team "The Seven."

00:01:40.609 --> 00:01:46.200
He recruits the young Hughie after the superhero
speedster A-Train unintentionally kills Hughie's

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.099
girlfriend Robin by running through her at
super speed.

00:01:49.099 --> 00:01:53.599
Simon Pegg appears in a recurring role as
Hughie's father fitting, since Pegg was the

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.560
inspiration for the comic book's Hughie.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:00.299
Judging by the action-packed and darkly funny
trailers, The Boys promises to be just as

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:03.609
unapologetically bloody and hilarious as the
source material.

00:02:03.609 --> 00:02:05.069
Check it out on July 26th.

00:02:06.069 --> 00:02:11.019
Just as Gotham's penultimate season came to
an end in May 2018, fans of the Dark Knight

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.920
learned that it wouldn't be the last Batman-related
prequel series on television.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:19.930
The premium cable network Epix ordered ten
episodes of Pennyworth, a series taking its

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:22.660
name from Batman's famous butler Alfred Pennyworth.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.020
While Pennyworth and Gotham don't exist within
the same universe, it seems likely putting

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:30.160
the spotlight on Gotham's Alfred helped make
Pennyworth a reality.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.960
Set in 1960s London, Pennyworth gives us a
much younger Alfred than we're used to, played

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:35.960
by Jack Bannon.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.360
"You can find a position in a good household.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.340
Do right, you're a butler before you're 40."

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:45.980
Fresh out of the British SAS, Pennyworth starts
a security company and his connections to

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:50.280
the larger story we already know are forged
when he's hired by Thomas Wayne, the doomed

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.440
father whose death will eventually lead to
the rise of Batman.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.680
Pennyworth's trailer looks fun, sexy, and
thrilling, and definitely worth a look when

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.940
the first season hits Prime on July 28th.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.660
Those are the major highlights now, let's
take a look at what else Amazon is offering,

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:04.660
genre-by-genre.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.920
July is injecting a lot of Star Trek into
Amazon Prime.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:14.840
Five Star Trek films come to the service on
July 31st, including 1996's Star Trek: First

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:19.220
Contact, which was the first of the films
to star only the crew of the Star Trek: The

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.170
Next Generation series.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:26.540
Directed by Jonathan Frakes aka William Riker
First Contact brought the popular cybernetic

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:30.180
hive-mind bad guys the Borg to the big screen
for the first time.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.680
If you're not interested in the future, a
number of Amazon's July action offerings delve

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:35.600
into the past.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:41.360
John Cusack and Emile Hirsch face off in the
gritty western Never Grow Old on July 13th.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:45.579
On July 31st you can see the acclaimed New
Zealand-made action-thriller Tracker.

00:03:45.579 --> 00:03:49.719
Ray Winstone plays a master tracker from the
South African side of the Second Boer War

00:03:49.719 --> 00:03:54.489
tasked with finding and capturing a man accused
of murdering a British soldier.

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:58.299
It flopped in the theaters and was roasted
by critics, but if you're still curious, the

00:03:58.299 --> 00:04:02.879
new Hellboy reboot, starring Stranger Things
fan favorite David Harbour, also hits the

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.360
streaming service on July 23rd, just a few
months after its theatrical release.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:13.840
Thriller and horror offerings bring mystery,
time travel, demons, and devil babies to Amazon

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:14.460
Prime in July.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.980
On the more thrilling side of things, Ben
Affleck's critically adored mystery Gone Baby

00:04:18.989 --> 00:04:23.410
Gone arrives on Prime on July 12th, while
at the end of the month, Bruce Willis travels

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:27.800
through time to save the world from Brad Pitt
in 1995's Twelve Monkeys.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.770
If you're looking for a hit of pure '90s nostalgia,
Hackers hits Prime on July 31st.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:37.000
Prime isn't short on the bloodier fare either,
though a lot of the scarier stuff doesn't

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.440
land until the very end of the month.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:44.660
On July 29th, viewers can watch The Haunting
of Sharon Tate, based on the infamous 1969

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:45.670
Manson Family murders.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:50.940
The last day of the month brings to Prime
the 2009 slasher remake My Bloody Valentine,

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:55.520
Jeepers Creepers 2, and the 1968 horror classic
Rosemary's Baby.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:00.820
After Peterloo, Amazon's drama offerings are
scarce, but what they lack in quantity they

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.000
make up for in quality.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:07.460
Ironically, two icy films premiering on Prime
at the end of July are about things starting

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.720
to get dark and cold.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.760
Starting July 28th, Prime subscribers can
watch After Darkness starring Natalia Dyer

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:17.240
of Stranger Things fame, and former Closer
lead Kyra Sedgwick.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:21.800
The sun is dying, and as the world grows dark,
a family prays for rescue while facing a few

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.280
skeletons in the closet.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:27.099
On the final day of July, the survival drama
Arctic appears on Prime.

00:05:27.099 --> 00:05:31.710
Mads Mikkelsen stars in the Icelandic film
as a man struggling to survive after his plane

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.120
crashes in the Arctic Circle.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:42.040
Also at the very end of July, Tim Burton's
stop-motion musical comedy Corpse Bride arrives

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:42.700
on Prime.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:47.660
When young Victor practices his wedding vows,
he's overheard by the Corpse Bride, who inexplicably

00:05:47.669 --> 00:05:50.970
believes the vows were meant for her, and
that the two are now married.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:55.539
The darkly funny ghost story was nominated
for an Oscar for Best Animated Feature in

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:56.040
2005.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:01.940
On July 21st, Prime subscribers can watch
Time Freak, a sci-fi comedy about the misadventures

00:06:01.949 --> 00:06:03.780
of a young physics prodigy.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:07.280
After the genius is dumped by his girlfriend
Debbie, played by Game of Thrones' Sophie

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:11.990
Turner, he invents a time machine and goes
back in time over and over again to try to

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.880
figure out what went wrong with Debbie and
fix the relationship.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:16.860
"You don't think I love you?"

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:18.160
"I don't know!

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:23.800
I know I said it, and then you ran off and
you came back and sang a song about a monkey."

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.240
Arctic isn't the only thing Iceland is sending
Amazon Prime in July.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:32.560
On July 10th, the second season of the Icelandic
mystery drama Trapped will be available for

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:33.560
streaming.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:37.800
Season 1 was about the police chief searching
for a killer after a mutilated torso surfaces

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:38.460
in the local harbor.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:43.310
Having moved to Iceland's capital Reykjavik
after the events of the first season, Season

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:47.729
2 finds the chief forced to return to his
hometown when a local politician is assaulted.

00:06:47.729 --> 00:06:52.340
Trapped's first season earned an impressive
100% critical rating on Rotten Tomatoes with

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:55.599
its audience rating of 97% not far behind.

00:06:55.599 --> 00:06:57.680
Ceri Radford of the Telegraph writes,

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:02.159
"Even without all these promising plot angles,
Trapped was worth watching for its chill beauty

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:02.660
alone."

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.080
Sounds like a cool way to spend a hot summer
night.

